  "body": "The fixed PR1062 11,500-ADD bit word has a frame-zero D that temporarily mixes helpers, so the inherited checker reports its documented H2/K syntax failures. This package supplies and proves a replacement scalar contract: D must preserve arbitrary sources/helpers and target basis, adding exactly N times the original helper inputs; semantic N must equal the actual raw helper-response K. H1/H3/H4/H5 and the U/J/C checks remain enforced.\n\nTwo different engines agree on all 661 D columns. A proof-only original-D splice passes all original interface flags; equality of the two zero-frame D prefixes leaves the subsequent literal chronological continuation unchanged. The unchanged predecessor checker, literal forward/reverse COPY/ERASE replay, complete local paid-profile recount and strict precision guards pass within the stated scope. The profile remains unchanged, with 9 rank-seven copies/erasures and rank mass 5129; the existing 95/182-bit bounds remain below 104/192. No new ADD saving or kappa is attributed here.\n\n~~~text\npython -I -O -B research/r439-semantic-d-contract-seed10/verify.py\npython -I -O -B research/r439-semantic-d-contract-seed10/test_package.py\n~~~\n\nSeven semantic controls plus five packaging corruptions and minimal relocation accompany the exact sources and 111-row compensation certificate. The module-level substitution proof does not replace native, physical/common-frame, precision/tape or hosting obligations; no selected supplier adoption is claimed. Contributor @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance, Apache-2.0, and full PR425/555/589/926/967/1015/923/1062 attribution.\n",
